+# Model-stall burden and fresh-session context savings — primary-evidence investigation
+
+**Office:** Ministry of Economy (Act 29). **Time:** 2026-11-24T19:05Z.
+**Trigger:** Founder operational inquiry quoting the 18:57:31Z read-only 24 h `session_v2` snapshot.
+**Type:** resource/efficiency evidence and one proposal. Not law, ballot, permit, activation,
+dispatch, staffing instruction, spending authority or a Judiciary finding. No model was
+dispatched, no live probe was issued, no config or state file was changed, no money spent.
+
+## 1. Source, scope and reproduction
+
+Primary source: the **main** Antonina OpenCode service DB at `$OPENCODE_DB`
+(`/home/lubko/.local/state/antonina/opencode-service/opencode.db`), opened with a
+`mode=ro` URI and `PRAGMA query_only=1`. The stopped secondary's 18-session DB at
+`~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db` is a different file and was **not** used. No live
+probe was attempted: the canonical guard forbids noncanonical live probes, and the
+secondary is stopped; the main service was left intact.
+
+Window `2026-11-23T18:57:31Z .. 2026-11-24T18:57:31Z` on `time_created` (ms):
+
+| Measure | Reproduced | Founder's snapshot |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| New sessions | 643 | 644 |
+| idle_outcome succeeded / failed / interrupted / null (session row) | 602 / 9 / 14 / 18 | 598 / 9 / 15 / 22 |
+| Cost sum | 0.0 | 0 |
+| Cache-read tokens | 3,432,097,655 | >3 B |
+
+The one-session and small outcome deltas are boundary conventions at the same instant;
+the findings below are insensitive to them. **Cache-read is 96.2 % of all 3,567,733,985
+accounting tokens**; `tokens_cache_write = 0`. This is the dominant measurable cost.
+
+## 2. Model-stall burden (primary evidence, not publication counts)
+
+**The final-model field is not attribution.** Of 643 sessions, **131 (20.4 %) actually
+used more than one distinct model** in `session_message` assistant records, and 137 had
+at least one `model-switched` message (**289 switches in the window**). Example:
+`ses_df6151a9bffe6RxeAEcjJZF9jU` records final `opencode-go/iceman-contributor-free` but
+actually called `opencode-go/hy4-flash-free` first. Typical switches are between free Go
+routes (`beam-free:low -> hy4-flash-free:low` 29×, `hy4-flash-free:default ->
+hungerg-free:-` 28×) — free-tier cooldown/fallback rotations, not progress.
+
+**Actual per-call attribution** (22,092 assistant messages in the window):
+
+| Model | Calls |
+|---|---:|
+| opencode-go/hy4-flash-free | 12,272 (55.6 %) |
+| opencode-go/hungerg-free | 3,047 |
+| opencode/hy4-flash-free | 2,647 |
+| opencode-go/beam-free | 2,131 |
+| opencode-go/iceman-contributor-free | 664 |
+| openai/gpt-6-luna | 141 (0.6 %) |
+
+By provider: **opencode-go 18,115 (82.0 %)**, opencode 3,836 (17.4 %), openai 141 (0.6 %).
+The "prefer robust Go free routes / Luna before paid" ladder is therefore already what
+runs; no route deletion or reorder is warranted by this evidence.
+
+**Variant gap:** 19,690 calls (89.1 %) recorded variant `default`; only 2,402 (10.9 %)
+recorded `low`, although every configured entry carries `variant: low`. This is a runtime
+behaviour, consistent with the standing incident record; it is reported, not silently
+"fixed" by relaxing the low-effort requirement.
+
+**Stall events (38 failed idle records in 28 sessions):** `provider.free-limit` 17,
+`provider.transport` 14, `provider.no-route` 4, `provider.quota` 1,
+`provider.rate-limit` 1, `provider.invalid-request` 1 (input 266,527 > 262,144 context
+limit). Plus **160 interrupted idle records in 107 sessions**. The `no-route` cases are
+the forced-low rejection on `opencode-go/iceman-contributor-free`; 6 switches went
+`iceman-contributor-free:low -> gpt-6-luna:low`, i.e. a low-variant rejection drove
+fallback toward the Luna tier. Sessions with a model-switch carried 2.56 B cache-read;
+sessions with an interrupted idle carried 1.73 B — stalls and long contexts co-occur,
+but a failed/no-route call burns no tokens itself. The honest burden of stalls is
+**fallback churn, wall-clock and quota pressure**, while the token burden lives in the
+long sessions that also stall (137 switch sessions = 74.7 % of all cache-read).
+
+Funding context at 18:41Z: 4 free models available, `failover_risk=elevated`,
+`provider_concentration=true` (only opencode-go), many free routes cooling until
+2026-11-25T00:53Z; sole fallback `openai/gpt-6-luna`. Cooldowns are respected, not bypassed.
+
+## 3. Fresh-session context savings (primary evidence)
+
+Cache-read per input-token ratio scales with session length:
+
+| Assistant messages / session | Sessions | Cache-read | cache_read / input |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 1 (fresh single turn) | 219 | 0.8 M | 1.5× |
+| 6–20 | 119 | 83.5 M | 8.6× |
+| 21–100 | 268 | 1,146 M | 20.6× |
+| 101+ | 32 | 2,214 M | 42.1× |
+
+**300 long sessions (21+ messages) hold 3.36 B cache-read = 98 % of all cache-read.**
+Largest single session: `ses_df37a0b2fffeaRPK5ul5lU7s9k`, 376.3 M cache-read, 777
+assistant messages, 169 min; maximum observed lifespan 548 min. A fresh single-turn
+session costs ~3.6 K cache-read. Auto-compaction is not a reliable backstop: in the
+window only 4 compactions completed and 4 failed (2 interrupted, 1 context-length
+invalid-request, 1 free-limit), and one session hit the hard 262,144-token ceiling.
+
+Conclusion: the dominant, measurable, avoidable cost is **re-reading accumulated context
+in long sessions**, not model stalls. This is a token/resource fact; it is **not** an
+inference about task success or publication counts.
+
+## 4. One proposed efficiency action
+
+**Adopt a measured fresh-session handover trigger for routine office rounds:** start a
+fresh session with a short handover note when a session's accumulated cache-read passes
+roughly 10 M tokens (or ~100 assistant turns), instead of relying on auto-compaction.
+This operationalizes the standing Fresh sessions directive with a concrete, falsifiable
+threshold. It applies to routine office rounds only — **not** to delegated research
+agents whose unfinished proof work genuinely needs context continuity.
+
+- **Estimated saving:** a bounded upper estimate of ~2.5–2.7 B cache-read tokens/day if
+  the 300 long sessions were split into handover-linked fresh sessions (fresh turns cost
+  ~3.6 K each). The conservative primary fact is the 98 % concentration and the 42:1
+  ratio; the projection assumes a handover note costs on the order of the 6–20-message
+  band (~0.7 M), and should be confirmed by a small controlled comparison before being
+  treated as a committed saving.
+- **Risk:** a handover note must preserve state or work is lost; input tokens rise
+  slightly; some tool-heavy work benefits from retained context. No staffing counts,
+  concurrency limits or project selection are prescribed — this is a resource mitigation
+  for the Executive to decide and implement, not a staffing instruction.
+- **Alternatives rejected on the evidence:** no route deletion (iceman-contributor-free
+  stays authorized, no-route diagnosed not removed); no cooldown bypass; no relaxation of
+  `low`; Luna stays before paid; no new free-route probe (canonical guard) and no probe of
+  the stopped secondary; no paid spend.
+
+## 5. What was deliberately not redone
+
+The first-wave Act34 post-landing attestation is finished and landed
+(`records/economy/2026-11-24-act34-post-landing-attestation.md`, delivered in
+`2a2d9ef5`); this investigation does not repeat or amend it. No config, model-policy,
+state file or law was changed. No live probe was issued. No money was spent.
+
+**Founder request:** none from this evidence alone. No reserved Founder authority or
+external authorization is needed; the single action is an Economy→Executive efficiency
+proposal.
